@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api

### SECTION 1: USER REGISTRATION & LOGIN

### Register a new user (Admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin_user",
  "email": "admin@test.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

### Register a new Manager
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "manager_user",
  "email": "manager@test.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

### Register a regular User
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "regular_user",
  "email": "user@test.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

### Login (Admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@test.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

### Login (Manager)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manager@test.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

### Login (Regular User)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@test.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}


### SECTION 2: TOKEN REFRESH

### Refresh Token (Use the refreshToken from login response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh?refreshToken=<PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE>


### SECTION 3: PUBLIC ENDPOINTS

### Public endpoint (No auth required)
GET {{baseUrl}}/test/public


### SECTION 4: AUTHENTICATED ENDPOINTS (Any logged-in user)

### Protected endpoint - Get current user info
GET {{baseUrl}}/test/me
Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE>

### Protected endpoint - Generic
GET {{baseUrl}}/test/protected
Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE>


### SECTION 5: ROLE-BASED ACCESS CONTROL (RBAC)

### Admin only endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/test/admin
Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE>

### Admin or Manager endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/test/management
Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_ADMIN_OR_MANAGER_TOKEN_HERE>

### Secure Admin endpoint (Policy-based)
GET {{baseUrl}}/test/secure-admin
Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE>


### SECTION 6: PERMISSION-BASED ENDPOINTS

### CanRead permission (Admin, Manager, User have this)
GET {{baseUrl}}/test/read-data
Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_TOKEN_HERE>

### CanWrite permission (Admin, Manager have this)
POST {{baseUrl}}/test/write-data
Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_TOKEN_HERE>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Data",
  "value": 123
}

### CanDelete permission (Only Admin has this)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/test/delete-data/123
Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE>

### CanManageUsers permission (Admin, Manager have this)
GET {{baseUrl}}/test/manage-users
Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_ADMIN_OR_MANAGER_TOKEN_HERE>


### SECTION 7: ERROR SCENARIOS

### Invalid credentials
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@test.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword"
}

### User not found
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@test.com",
  "password": "anypassword"
}

### Try accessing protected endpoint without token (should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/test/protected

### Try accessing admin endpoint as regular user (should fail with admin token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/test/admin
Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_USER_TOKEN_HERE>

### Try accessing write endpoint as user (should fail - user only has read permission)
POST {{baseUrl}}/test/write-data
Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_USER_TOKEN_HERE>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "data": "test"
}
